      "side": 1,
      "message": "1) push_bazel_apps does not use the Docker image of the infra repo - it checks out the infra repo at ToT (by default) and runs bazel_release_ci. \n\n2) It tags pushed image with the githash that was passed in via --skia_revision, which controls which skia-wasm-release image to use as the source. I was not clear on the benefits of deploying a non-checked in version (i.e. a Tryjob version) of the wasm products, so I made it easiest to just push images built from checked in code. We can control this via the --skia_revision flag, which is set via gen_tasks_logic.\n\nNo changes needed to docker_pushes_watcher.",
